1961 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Once you take the piece off the loom\054 you will be left with 66 warp thread tails to hide or secure\056 Hiding them all can easily take a whole day\054 keeping the overall process somewhat slow\056\nI don\047t really know how to speed it up\054 but at least there is a trick to lengthen these tails\054 making them more comfortable to weave in or knot\056 Set up your warp threads as shown in the second photo\072 warp the loom in one continuous\054 huge spiral for 33 full rounds\056 Once cut\054 they will give you plenty of length to work with\056)
     /K [ 4 ]
     /P 1962 0 R
     /Pg 1181 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

